        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "6bfa03d9-08d5-5561-b590-7a92b1b8ed31",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: United States Coast Guard, War Shipping Administration, National Bulk Carriers\n- Places: Chatham, Massachusetts, Portland, Oregon, United States\n- Products: United States Coast Guard Station Chatham, SS Pendleton, SS Fort Mercer, The Finest Hours\n- Events: 1952 Pendleton rescue\n- People: Michael J. Tougias, Chris Pine\n\nFacts:\n- SS Pendleton was a Type T2-SE-A1 tanker built in 1944 in Portland, Oregon, United States, for the War Shipping Administration.\n- SS Pendleton was sold in 1948 to National Bulk Carriers.\n- In February 1952, SS Pendleton broke in two in a storm.\n- United States Coast Guard Station Chatham is a United States Coast Guard station in Chatham, Massachusetts.\n- United States Coast Guard Station Chatham was the origin of the famous 1952 Pendleton rescue.\n- The sinking of SS Pendleton and the rescue of its crew, along with the break-up and rescue of its sister ship SS Fort Mercer, are the subject of Michael J. Tougias's 2009 book The Finest Hours: The True Story Behind the US Coast Guard's Most Daring Rescue.\n- Michael J. Tougias's book inspired the 2016 film The Finest Hours starring Chris Pine, which focuses on the Pendleton rescue.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "e863f494-9598-511d-be94-d3a70e6dfbe8",
        "text": "Page: Coast Guard Station Chatham. Sentence: United States Coast Guard Station Chatham is a United States Coast Guard station located in Chatham, Massachusetts.\nPage: Coast Guard Station Chatham. Sentence: The station was the origin of the famous 1952 Pendleton rescue.\nPage: SS Pendleton. Sentence: SS \"Pendleton\" was a Type T2-SE-A1 tanker built in 1944 in Portland, Oregon, United States, for the War Shipping Administration.\nPage: SS Pendleton. Sentence: She was sold in 1948 to National Bulk Carriers, serving until February 1952 when she broke in two in a storm.\nPage: SS Pendleton. Sentence: The ship's sinking and crew rescue (along with break-up and rescue of its sister ship the \"SS Fort Mercer\") is the topic of the 2009 book \"The Finest Hours: The True Story Behind the US Coast Guard's Most Daring Rescue\", by Michael J. Tougias.\nPage: SS Pendleton. Sentence: Tougias' book inspired the 2016 film \"The Finest Hours\" with Chris Pine, which focuses on the \"Pendelton\" rescue.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
